  "_comment": [
    "Test vectors for the kubeconfig mint seal (packages/core/kubeaccess/seal.go, #5280).",
    "Consumed by seal_test.go and, later, by the browser (WebCrypto) open implementation, which must pass both.",
    "rfc9180: HPKE base mode, DHKEM(X25519, HKDF-SHA256) / HKDF-SHA256 / AES-256-GCM (0x0020/0x0001/0x0002), from the CFRG test-vectors.json the RFC 9180 appendix is generated from (github.com/cfrg/draft-irtf-cfrg-hpke, test-vectors.json, sha256 61fc662f01996cd06d713dacf5e133167bd309a1f329442d53f1e21a47b3ede6). RFC 9180 Appendix A prints this KEM/KDF only with AES-128-GCM and ChaCha20Poly1305; this AES-256-GCM entry is the same file's. pkRm/skRm/enc match Go's crypto/hpke testdata/rfc9180.json for this suite. Only the first two encryptions and the first export are kept; all hex.",
    "alethia_mint: one real seal under the Alethia construction (info = 'alethia/kubeconfig-mint/v1', aad = info || 0x00 || mint_id || 0x00 || cluster_id). The recipient key is DeriveKeyPair(recipient_ikm). The blob was produced once by Seal (random ephemeral) and frozen; opening it with recipient_sk, mint_id and cluster_id must yield plaintext exactly, and opening it with any other id must fail."
  ],
